A||||4||Daleford||Where do I buy weld-your-own-wheels?||||5||
Z||000000||Daleford||11-03-2001||10:26 PM||||I play with kitcars. I need a source for wheel shells. [wheel with rim only, center separate]  Centers can then be welded in where we need them for the proper offset.<BR>I used to buy wheel shells when I was stockcar racing, but can't find anything larger than 15 inch from raceshops.  Would want at least 16 inch.   Anybody help?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||11-04-2001||12:12 AM||||HRE will custom make any size from 14"-20" in any offset or bolt pattern from their 12 or so styles.  Very pricey, though at around $500USD/each and up.  Can't see where any car is worth more than 2 grand in wheels alone (but what do I know?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ).||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||11-04-2001||12:30 AM||||I know lots of companies will custom make wheels with your dimensions.  One that has great prices, if you like their styles, is Centerline.  You have to wait a while, but it's well worth it for custom sizes in an application like yours.  If you aren't sure what measurements you want to use and want to weld your own specifically because of that reason, I can't help you.  I'd think it would be better to mock something up to get the measurements you need, then get them custom made.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-04-2001||06:27 AM||||Too much can go wrong if you assemble your own wheels.  Your balance could be off alot or your wheel center could be crooked.  It wouldn't take much for you to either destroy a wheel or have it come apart at speed.  Keep in mind that pro racers (NASCAR, Indy, F1, etc) don't manufacture their own wheels.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Daleford||11-04-2001||10:03 AM||||Thanks for the input, guys.  Anybody else?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||14
